/*
Problem: Merge Strings Alternately
Platform: LeetCode (LC 1768)
Topic: String / Two Pointers

---------------------------------------------------------

Approach:

Given two strings:

word1
word2

Merge them by taking characters
alternately from each string.

If one string becomes exhausted,
append the remaining characters
of the other string.

---------------------------------------------------------

Two Pointer Idea:

Maintain:

i -> current index in word1
j -> current index in word2

Traverse both strings simultaneously.

---------------------------------------------------------

Algorithm:

While both strings still have characters:

1. Add word1[i]
2. Add word2[j]
3. Increment both pointers

---------------------------------------------------------

After one string ends:

If word1 still has characters:

Append all remaining characters.

If word2 still has characters:

Append all remaining characters.

---------------------------------------------------------

Example 1:

Input:

word1 = "abc"
word2 = "pqr"

Process:

a + p
b + q
c + r

Answer:

"apbqcr"

---------------------------------------------------------

Example 2:

Input:

word1 = "ab"
word2 = "pqrs"

Process:

a + p
b + q

word1 finished.

Append remaining:

r s

Answer:

"apbqrs"

---------------------------------------------------------

Example 3:

Input:

word1 = "abcd"
word2 = "pq"

Process:

a + p
b + q

word2 finished.

Append remaining:

c d

Answer:

"apbqcd"

---------------------------------------------------------

Time Complexity: O(n + m)

n = word1.length()
m = word2.length()

Every character is visited exactly once.

---------------------------------------------------------

Space Complexity: O(n + m)

The answer string stores all characters.

---------------------------------------------------------
*/

class Solution {
public:
    string mergeAlternately(string word1,
                            string word2) {

        int i = 0;
        int j = 0;

        string ans = "";

        // Merge while both strings have characters
        while (i < word1.size() &&
               j < word2.size()) {

            ans += word1[i];
            ans += word2[j];

            i++;
            j++;
        }

        // Append remaining characters of word1
        while (i < word1.size()) {

            ans += word1[i];

            i++;
        }

        // Append remaining characters of word2
        while (j < word2.size()) {

            ans += word2[j];

            j++;
        }

        return ans;
    }
};
